CORE
main.py
--python-unbounded-ints --unwind 12

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
List literals, indexing, and range comprehensions must work under
--python-unbounded-ints. The list length/array-dimension are always
signedbv[64] (matching python_list_type), while elements and iteration
values take the python int type (integer_typet here) so they compose
with int literals. Range comprehension args are recognised as
integer_typet. Previously these crashed (SSA type-mismatch) or
produced a wrong length.
